{
  "_doc": "Edit lists for tools/video/cut.py. format 16x9 | 9x16. A segment is a card (store picture or colour, with text) or footage: take (reports/video/raw/<take>), t (seconds into the take's joined file; `cut.py sheets` labels every 2 s), dur, speed (>1 = faster, <1 = slow motion), fit (blur: the whole view, a blurred copy fills the frame, the default; fill: crop to the frame), zoom (with blur: >1 crops into the middle of the view), shift (with blur: move the view down, share of the height), y (top of the text, share of the height). Text: tag (step label), title (big), sub (smaller line), color (tag colour; title colour on a card). takes: fixes per take (mask: [x, y, w, h] boxes in the joined file's pixels blurred away; top: share of the height cut off).",
